title: Who can see what › Roles, sites and a record at the other site
route: Every page (top bar, Demo menu › Viewing as)
intro: A clinic can run more than one site, and staff at one site must not see the other site's patients (minimum necessary access). The demo has Site A and Site B and four viewers. What a viewer may see sets the sites in view, and every screen reads it.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: the viewer is chosen in the Demo menu. In a real clinic it follows the person who signs in. Payers, agents and Settings are clinic-wide and do not follow the site.
---
start s1 "Psyflo opens\nDefault viewer: Jordan Perez, UR coordinator, on Both sites"

group gRoles "The four demo viewers (src/data/viewers.ts)"
  process r1 "Jordan Perez, UR coordinator\nSite A and Site B"
  process r2 "Alex Morgan, clinic owner\nSite A and Site B"
  process r3 "Dr. Rivera, clinician\nSite A only"
  process r4 "Sam Okafor, billing\nSite B only"
endgroup

click cView "Choose a viewer\nDemo menu › 'Viewing as', or Settings › Sites and access › 'View as'"
goto gView "Continues in: Global shell › Demo menu › Viewing as"
decision d1 "May this viewer see both sites?"

group gBoth "Both sites"
  screen tb1 "Top bar shows the switch\n'Both sites | Site A | Site B'\nStarts on 'Both sites'"
  input pick "Choose 'Both sites', 'Site A' or 'Site B'"
  goto gSw "Continues in: Global shell › Top bar › Site switcher"
endgroup

group gOne "One site only"
  screen tb2 "Top bar shows a locked label\n'Site A only' or 'Site B only', with an info note on why"
  process one "There is no 'Both sites' choice and nothing to switch"
endgroup

process view "The view is the sites chosen (or the one site the viewer may see)"
store site "Every case belongs to a site\nsiteOf(case id): the headline cases are placed by hand, every other id by a stable hash\nThe same case is at the same site on every screen"
process read "Every screen reads the view\nLists, counts, sidebar badges, charts, search, pickers, notifications, Ask FLO answers, exports"
process sum "Site A plus Site B always equals Both sites\nIn the default view every number is as it was before sites"

decision d2 "Is the record the person opens inside the view?"
screen rec "The record opens as usual"
screen oos "Notice: 'This case is not available at Site A'\nIt names no patient. It says which site the record belongs to and which sites this viewer can see"
decision d3 "Can this viewer see the record's site?"
click showSite "Click 'Show Site B'\n(only for a viewer who may see both sites)"
process sw2 "The view becomes the record's site"
click back "Click 'Back to the Dashboard'"
endx stop "The one-site viewer cannot reach the other site's record from any screen, link or search"

group gWide "Not site data: clinic-wide"
  process cw1 "Payers: rules, documents and changes are the clinic's\nThe Payers badge never changes with the view"
  process cw2 "Agents and Settings: the sixteen agents and Pause all"
  process cw3 "Payer changes: 'Update N drafts' counts only the drafts in the view"
endgroup

group gEmr "Per site"
  process e1 "EMR Connect: each site has its own clinical record system\nThe billing system serves both\nA one-site viewer sees and changes only their own"
endgroup

goto gOut "Continues in: EMR Connect › Page › Arrive and read the page"
end e1x "Each viewer works only with the patients at their site"

s1 --> r1 & r2 & r3 & r4
r1 & r2 & r3 & r4 --> d1
s1 --> cView --> gView
d1 -->|Yes| tb1 --> pick --> gSw
d1 -->|No| tb2 --> one
pick --> view
one --> view
view --> site --> read --> sum
read --> d2
d2 -->|Yes| rec --> e1x
d2 -->|No| oos --> d3
d3 -->|Yes| showSite --> sw2 --> rec
d3 -->|No| back
back --> stop
read -.-> cw1 & cw2 & cw3
read -.-> e1
e1 --> gOut
